From 92ec77a385f189cb65bae3c94641cb7318a56094 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:16:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: ti: omap: espresso-common: keep the WLAN powered in
 suspend

brcmfmac keeps the BCM4330 powered across system suspend and needs the
SDIO host to allow that (MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER). Without
keep-power-in-suspend on mmc5, suspend logs

  brcmfmac: brcmf_ops_sdio_suspend: Failed to set pm_flags 1

the MMC core powers the card down anyway, and after resume the driver
talks to a chip that lost its firmware:

  brcmfmac: brcmf_sdio_htclk: HT Avail request error: -110

endlessly, with Wi-Fi gone until a reboot.

Let the host keep the card powered in suspend.

Fixes: f768d54723d1 ("ARM: dts: ti: omap: espresso-common: Add common device tree for Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 series")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
index 28c54f1b5738..47220a2d9889 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
@@ -921,6 +921,7 @@ &mmc5 {
 	#size-cells = <0>;
 
 	non-removable;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_espresso_wlan>;
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wlan_pwrseq>;
-- 
2.55.0

